      "explanation": "Higher the value of K<sub>a</sub> or lower the value pK<sub>a</sub>,  stronger will be the acid.\n<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1leyjxg71/da9290ce-b0ce-486d-95bc-46b5ca8813b8/3b023ed0-bd11-11ed-89dd-7deceac5f9ee/file-1leyjxg72.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1leyjxg71/da9290ce-b0ce-486d-95bc-46b5ca8813b8/3b023ed0-bd11-11ed-89dd-7deceac5f9ee/file-1leyjxg72.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2023 (Online) 30th January Evening Shift Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 70 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1leyjxg71/da9290ce-b0ce-486d-95bc-46b5ca8813b8/3b023ed0-bd11-11ed-89dd-7deceac5f9ee/file-1leyjxg72.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1leyjxg71/da9290ce-b0ce-486d-95bc-46b5ca8813b8/3b023ed0-bd11-11ed-89dd-7deceac5f9ee/file-1leyjxg72.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1leyjxg71/da9290ce-b0ce-486d-95bc-46b5ca8813b8/3b023ed0-bd11-11ed-89dd-7deceac5f9ee/file-1leyjxg72.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1leyjxg71/da9290ce-b0ce-486d-95bc-46b5ca8813b8/3b023ed0-bd11-11ed-89dd-7deceac5f9ee/file-1leyjxg72.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1leyjxg71/da9290ce-b0ce-486d-95bc-46b5ca8813b8/3b023ed0-bd11-11ed-89dd-7deceac5f9ee/file-1leyjxg72.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1leyjxg71/da9290ce-b0ce-486d-95bc-46b5ca8813b8/3b023ed0-bd11-11ed-89dd-7deceac5f9ee/file-1leyjxg72.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<br>Presence of electron donating groups destabilises the  phonoxide ion, thus, reduces acidic nature of phenol.  Presence of electron withdrawing group stabilises the  phenoxide ion thus increase the acidic strength of phenol.  \n<br><br>Thus, order of acidic strength is:\n<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1leyjyrce/d124cdcf-c789-49ee-a061-57387fd5d3ee/5f6e20e0-bd11-11ed-8584-0da66617294d/file-1leyjyrcf.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1leyjyrce/d124cdcf-c789-49ee-a061-57387fd5d3ee/5f6e20e0-bd11-11ed-8584-0da66617294d/file-1leyjyrcf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2023 (Online) 30th January Evening Shift Chemistry - Alcohols, Phenols and Ethers Question 70 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1leyjyrce/d124cdcf-c789-49ee-a061-57387fd5d3ee/5f6e20e0-bd11-11ed-8584-0da66617294d/file-1leyjyrcf.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1leyjyrce/d124cdcf-c789-49ee-a061-57387fd5d3ee/5f6e20e0-bd11-11ed-8584-0da66617294d/file-1leyjyrcf.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1leyjyrce/d124cdcf-c789-49ee-a061-57387fd5d3ee/5f6e20e0-bd11-11ed-8584-0da66617294d/file-1leyjyrcf.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1leyjyrce/d124cdcf-c789-49ee-a061-57387fd5d3ee/5f6e20e0-bd11-11ed-8584-0da66617294d/file-1leyjyrcf.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1leyjyrce/d124cdcf-c789-49ee-a061-57387fd5d3ee/5f6e20e0-bd11-11ed-8584-0da66617294d/file-1leyjyrcf.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1leyjyrce/d124cdcf-c789-49ee-a061-57387fd5d3ee/5f6e20e0-bd11-11ed-8584-0da66617294d/file-1leyjyrcf.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Order of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.537ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.006ex\" height=\"2.082ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1770.6 920.1\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"70\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-70\"></use><use data-c=\"4B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-4B\" transform=\"translate(556,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1367,-229.4) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"61\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-61\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> will be = b &gt; d &gt; a &gt; c</p>\n<p><b>Note :</b></p>\n<p>Acid Strength : -</p>\n<p>Acids : Acids are those molecules which donates H<sup>+</sup> ion in aqueous solution (water) and increases concentration of H<sup>+</sup> ion in water.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.469ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 4627.4 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1110.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\">